# CometGUI -- jpackage options shared by every platform (Phase 14, unit 5).
#
# A jpackage argument file: scripts/package/build-app-image.sh passes it as
# @packaging/jpackage/common.args, then the platform's own file, then the
# values only a build knows (--app-version from the build identity, --input,
# --main-jar, --add-modules from packaging/runtime-modules.txt, --dest).
# Lines starting with # are comments; a value with spaces is double-quoted.

--name CometGUI
--main-class org.cometgui.app.bootstrap.CometGuiLauncher
--vendor "The CometGUI authors"
--description "Comet to Percolator proteomics search workflow with provenance"
--copyright "Copyright (C) 2026 The CometGUI authors. GPL-3.0-only."

# THE RUNTIME KEEPS bin/java.  Without --jlink-options jpackage runs jlink with
# --strip-native-commands, and the bundled runtime has no java launcher at all
# (docs/feasibility/toolchain.rst, "The bundled runtime has no java launcher by
# default").  The product launches PDV and the Limelight converter -- both
# JARs -- from java.home/bin/java (org.cometgui.tools.api.JavaRuntime), so an
# image without it installs, starts, and then cannot run either tool.
# Supplying the option REPLACES jpackage's defaults; these are those defaults
# minus --strip-native-commands.
--jlink-options "--strip-debug --no-man-pages --no-header-files"

# NATIVE ACCESS, both measured on the packaged image on 2026-10-23.
#  ALL-UNNAMED: org.cometgui.app.config.FfmGlibcVersionSource calls
#    gnu_get_libc_version through java.lang.foreign from the class path
#    (cometgui-app/pom.xml records this option for the packaged application).
#  javafx.graphics: without it the launcher prints "WARNING: java.lang.System::load
#    has been called by com.sun.glass.utils.NativeLibLoader in module
#    javafx.graphics" at every start; the warning names this exact option.
--java-options --enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED
--java-options --enable-native-access=javafx.graphics

# NOT HERE, ON PURPOSE: -Dsun.jnu.encoding=UTF-8.  It is inert -- the JVM
# resolves sun.jnu.encoding from the process environment before system
# properties apply -- so it would be accepted and change nothing (STATUS.rst,
# "Risks currently live", item 1).  Starting the JVM in a UTF-8 locale is the
# packaged launcher's job and belongs to Phase 16; it cannot be expressed as a
# java option.  scripts/package/build-app-image.sh refuses an image whose
# launcher configuration mentions sun.jnu.encoding.
